@startuml Login and Attribution Process

title Process: giving a volunteer an account that can change things
caption Target design. Decisions O34, O35, O19. Plans 02 and 03.

|Volunteer|
start
:Sign in with the identity provider;

|Freedom|
if (Login linked to a person?) then (no)
  :Allow reads the roles permit;
  :Refuse every change that records who did it (403);
  |Administrator|
  :Open the volunteer's person record;
  :Link the login to the person;
  |Freedom|
  if (Login already linked to someone else?) then (yes)
    :Refuse the link (409);
    stop
  else (no)
    :Store the subject on the person's erasable details;
  endif
else (yes)
endif

|Volunteer|
:Make a change;

|Freedom|
:Take the person from the login, never from the request;
:Record who changed it and when, in the same write;

|Administrator|
if (Volunteer asks to be erased?) then (yes)
  :Erase the volunteer;
  |Freedom|
  :Delete personal details, including the login link;
  :Records that name them now read "Former volunteer";
else (no)
endif
stop

@enduml
